From 1b74545a5c6acbc7421efc34253b560fa3362a4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 07:34:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/58] Integration: term-index routing, entity-named blind
 verification, heartbeat snapshot rule, scale repairs

WP1 (claude-sonnet-5-5), reviewed fixes F1-F11 plus S1 minimum-unit attribution, evidence_freshness
meta, motivating_lineage redaction; H1 content-free term incidence (keyed hashes of rare terms from
PUBLIC records only, migration 0007_term_index, decision D18) used by rank_holders; H2 verification
questions name the claim's entity display names; H5 a heartbeat removes published domains/entities/
terms only on a vouched complete snapshot.
ENGINEER-E (claude-sonnet-5-5): bounded open holders with activation on inbox messages
(MYCELIC_MAX_OPEN_HOLDERS, default unlimited), per-holder lifecycle lock fixing the remove/ensure
dead-consumer race, trigger-maintained org/holder/taxonomy revision counters (migration 0006) keying
authz and routing caches, subject-indexed transport wake-ups. Measured at N=10,000 (coordinator):
candidate_holders 8.3 s -> 31-231 ms, question_audience 21.9 s -> 0.47 s.
Engineers' full-suite run on this tree: 496 passed, 7 skipped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
